    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0223" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/1075: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Forbes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-22T14:00:00+09:00">October 22, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 22—5:24 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>197. The Government yesterday instructed the Japanese Ambassadors in Italy and
                    France to address inquiries to the Governments to which they are respectively
                    accredited, and to express verbally the views which you outlined to Debuchi. I
                    understand that the text of Government’s instructions has been repeated to
                    Debuchi for your information.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d126-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Forbes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d126-f1" n="52" xml:id="d126-f1-content">
                <p>On October 30, the Japanese Ambassador reported to the Department the steps which
                    his Government had taken; memorandum of conversation not printed (500
                    A15a3/1219).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
